/-!
# `ErrorfLive` for the real format, satisfied by a position-independent stub (amd64)

The amd64 counterpart of `ErrorfRealImpl`: the stub generated by `scripts/errorf/gen_amd64.py` (prologue `mov r15, [rsp]`,
two decimal loops, one bump allocation, three copy loops, epilogue `add rsp, 8; jmp r15`), proven at `E0 = 2^46` for any
`tys`, `tErr`, `tInt`, `iE`, `iW`; the itab words are read from the runtime's constants cell (`ErrorfRealRt`).
`RelocAmd64.summary_transport64` moves it to a program's contract address (`ErrorfRealLive64`).
-/

